Assistant: The error occurs because we're trying to pass a function through postMessage in the iframe communication, which isn't allowed. Functions can't be cloned for postMessage. Let's modify the preview to use a plain object instead of a function for the table prop.

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/DynamicLink-60790d4b.tsx">
<change>
<description>Replace function with static data structure that can be cloned</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { DynamicLink } from '../../../../packages/features/users/components/UserTable/BulkActions/DynamicLink';

// Mock the required dependencies
const mockUseLocale = () => ({
  t: (key: string) => key,
});

const mockUseCopy = () => ({
  copyToClipboard: () => {},
  isCopied: false,
});

// Mock the nuqs hooks
const mockUseQueryState = () => [true, () => {}];

// Add global mocks
global["@calcom/lib/hooks/useLocale"] = mockUseLocale;
global["@calcom/lib/hooks/useCopy"] = mockUseCopy;
global["nuqs"] = {
  useQueryState: mockUseQueryState,
  parseAsBoolean: (value: any) => Boolean(value),
};

// Create a static table object that can be cloned
const createStaticTable = () => ({
  rows: [
    { original: { username: 'user1' } },
    { original: { username: 'user2' } }
  ],
  flatRows: [
    { original: { username: 'user1' } },
    { original: { username: 'user2' } }
  ],
  getSelectedRowModel: undefined as any
});

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    table: {
      type: 'object',
      value: createStaticTable(),
      label: 'Table',
    },
    domain: {
      type: 'string',
      value: 'https://example.com',
      label: 'Domain',
    },
  });

  // Create the table object with the method attached after the postMessage
  const tableWithMethods = {
    ...state.table.value,
    getSelectedRowModel: () => ({
      rows: state.table.value.rows,
      flatRows: state.table.value.flatRows,
    }),
  };

  return (
    <DynamicLink
      table={tableWithMethods as any}
      domain={state.domain.value}
    />
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

The changes made:

1. Created a static table object structure that can be safely cloned through postMessage
2. Moved the function definition out of the state object
3. Added the method back to the table object after the postMessage communication
4. Maintained the same data structure but in a way that can be properly serialized

This should resolve the DataCloneError while still providing the same functionality to the DynamicLink component. The key change is that we're no longer trying to pass functions through the iframe communication, instead passing only the data and reconstructing the methods afterward.

